TEXT -416 168 Left 4 ;Generator at isolated operation mode
TEXT -184 320 Left 2 ;For voltage regulation there is a AVR\nIt is enabled from 1s because then the\ngenerator output voltage reach their nominal\nvalue. You can see that the voltage drops at\nswitching the load and later is compensated\nby increasing the field voltage of the machine
TEXT -264 472 Left 2 ;Speed regulator is on at from the beginning\nAt 2s there is a load step of 100MW\nsee load angle V(u6:theta) of approx. 8 degrees\nStarting with 5s the load angle gets lower and lower since the\nconstant impedance loads voltage also gets lower and lower
TEXT -384 264 Left 2 ;Interner Lastwinkel =  V(u6:theta)
TEXT 40 384 Left 2 ;After 2s there is a load step of 100MW
TEXT 80 368 Left 2 !.param PN=100e6 QN=0
TEXT -320 536 Left 2 ;Nominal torque
TEXT -240 536 Left 2 ;Torque due to friqtion
TEXT -432 560 Left 2 ;The Rotational energy is J*omega_mech^2/2=100000*314.159/2*314.159/2/2=1.233GJ
TEXT -432 576 Left 2 ;This can be seen by view the power of the load (ALT+Click on the load)\n= is like plot (V(P002)*Ix(U1:L1)+V(P003)*Ix(U1:L2)+V(P004)*Ix(U1:L3))\nThen CTRL+click the tracename above to show the energy
TEXT -432 608 Left 2 ;NOTE: You have to manually set the x-axis from 5s to 90s before !!!!
TEXT -432 624 Left 2 ;The average power is about 14MW this means that the rotational energy\ncan deliver 14MW for 85s (or approx. 400MW= full load for 3s)
